{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1383865-other-national-totems","id":1383865,"title":"Other national Totems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-25T16:53:43-07:00","id":1383865,"title":"Other national Totems","content":"Has anyone done a custom totem for other national ideals like The American Dream or the New World Trinity? I was trying to think it it would be in good or bad taste for example to have a bunch of Silver Fangs who Followed Britania.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T17:11:16-07:00","id":1383871,"title":"","content":"National totems are probably a relatively recent phenomenon alongside the development of the nation state and thus the mythologizing of the nation and its history as would be necessary to imbue significant pathos to generate a powerful enough spirit.<br /> <br /> I'd say that most such spirits are probably localized to their regions of origin but stuff like: Mother Russia, Brittania, John Bull, The State, and so on. There's no doubt a Wikipedia article listing others.<br /> <br /> As far as taste goes, I can't say, but Silver Fangs would definitely have an affinity for the monarchy, although not always with the involved human institutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T05:00:45-07:00","id":1383941,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_personification\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a list of national personifications, there are some state and city ones (even bodies of water) as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T11:41:18-07:00","id":1383984,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider is that American Dream is more the embodiment of an ideal rather than of an actual geo-political entity. The embodiment of the United States as a nation-state would be Uncle Sam or Columbia. <br /> <br /> I think a parallel might be drawn between John Bull being more of an incarnation of the English or British everyman, while Britannia is an incarnation of Great Britain and/or the British Empire. <br /> <br /> Embodiments of nation states are likely to be something one step up from the City Father/Mother, but are also likely to be extremely Weaver oriented, increasingly tied to the aspect of Dogma (what used to be the Patriarchy, but in all honesty is likely Conformity now.) as the idea of Statism and blind obedience to government dictates continues to grow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:29:13-07:00","id":1384044,"title":"","content":"Good call that maybe the Nation Mothers/Fathers are maybe Weaver oriented.<br /> <br /> I think if they ever became popular some septs would maybe look down on them as some would view the Garou as needing to have loyalty to their mission with Gaia over things like human religions and nations, but Garou do them anyways, we have Garou Priests and Imams after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:51:58-07:00","id":1384046,"title":"","content":"I think the idea that the American Dream, New World Trinity.. hell All mighty Dollar and Easy credit can get out of being tied to the weaver but not say... the Spirit of the Revolution(Via la France!) is... very... um Americanocentric? No seriously nations are too weavery but not the embodiment of the Debt Economy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T16:58:20-07:00","id":1384057,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the spirit of revolution would be an aspect of the Totem The People (who refuses to accept both Red Talons for being too anti-human, and Glass Walkers for being too Weaver friendly). The People is a War Totem, dedicating its packs towards fighting oppression.<br /> <br /> This would be very different from a nation-level upgrade of a City Parent to the Nation Spirit of France. The People might stoke revolutions, but the governments that take over once the dust settles aren't necessarily fully committed to such principles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T18:55:14-07:00","id":1384069,"title":"","content":"I believe that spirits of national personification exist in the Umbra, but I would be leery of allowing Garou to have them as totems. For the same reasons, I've never really liked a lot of the pack totems already described in this thread.<br /> <br /> 1) They're taking the Garou away from an emphasis on Gaia.<br /> 2) At least cities can be considered their own ecosystem and represents a place rather than a people (as opposed to mere inhabitants) so I am not as opposed to City Fathers. (But I personally like the idea of urban packs interacting with such spirits, rather than having one as a pack or caern totem. Same thing for a totem like Tammany Hall - it should be a dangerous urban spirit that may or may not be helpful to Garou in the urban penumbra).<br /> 3) Since national characteristics (stereotypes) can be very controversial, I would think determining things like pack bonuses and bans could easily deteriorate OOC. That might be something a single game troupe wouldn't have problem with, but I think it wouldn't go over well in anything officially published.<br /> 4) Totems are best built around universal archetypes, and spirits of any nation, since its based on human culture, are not universal but very specific (and prone to change).<br /> <br /> I think a totem like the Sodals, despite being based on Weavery aspects of human culture, are more appropriate because it is very universal. It doesn't matter what kind of fraternal bond exists - it could be warrior brotherhoods, gang solidarity, labor unions on strike, religious orders, or college fraternities. It could even apply to those artificial packs created by wildlife workers who raise wolves and put them together to release into the wild.<br /> <br /> I'm less sold on something like the Invisible Hand, but at least that too can be interpreted quite universally. The concept of exchange is a very old one.<br /> <br /> I thought a totem like the American Dream was just a little too cute, and I didn't really think there were relevant for either the Bone Gnawers or Fianna. Likewise for the General Lee. And I don't think the New World Trinity really make much sense, but I can at least credit the writer of the Children of Gaia tribebook points for trying to be creative.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to give the strange totems found in the Glass Walker tribebooks more leeway simply because that tribe is supposed to be different from the other tribes, and have made chiminage to different kinds of spirits. But here I'd be more focused on technological totems rather than human cultural ones. So yes to Clashing Boom Boom, but not to Ole Mighty Dollar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:44:16-07:00","id":1384205,"title":"","content":"Some of the religion-of-state-type of deities depicted in the later supplements to <i>Scion 1e </i>would be a good starting point for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T00:11:59-07:00","id":1384372,"title":"","content":"I might have National Totems exist in the Umbra, but I don't think I'd ever have them adopt a tribe or caern, as the Garou's ultimate loyalty lies with the Garou Nation and not the human entities such spirits embody, which would seem to be a required aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:59:22-07:00","id":1384498,"title":"","content":"I'd agree that most garou likely wouldn't follow and would be hard pressed to acknowledge national totems, although I'd say that the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers might be exceptions to that rule, or at the very least those tribes would likely have camps or factions tied into them.<br /> <br /> The other tribes I agree are much less likely to acknowledge national totems, aside from perhaps the occasional homid-camps of tribes such as the Fianna or Fenrir who are known to maintain unfortunate ties to their human communities from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}